  "TourPoints": [
    {
      "Id": "bc17aa6c-699f-4343-9e64-1b475862a49c",
      "Description": "So far, float and integer values were used on their own.\nNow they are combined into vectors.\nA vector is a group of values that belong together."
    },
    {
      "Id": "494aa524-31fb-4fb6-bdb0-e9b7b314a078",
      "Description": "Depending on context, vector components can represent: - positions (x, y, z) - colors (r, g, b) - sizes (width, height)\nIn TiXL, vectors can have two, three, or four components and can use floating-point or integer values."
    },
    {
      "Id": "829f4cee-2135-4e21-ae31-862bd3e552cd",
      "Description": "Let’s start by building some vectors."
    },
    {
      "Id": "f00a84e8-ec27-49a5-8d58-3adc3bec3d4b",
      "Description": "Use [Vector3] to combine a noise value and an animation value.\nUse the result to control the position of a [Text] operator.\nFind the correct parameters to match the goal.",
      "Style": "CallToAction"
    }
  ]
}